{"id":"countries-katakana","name":"COUNTRIES","glyph":"ア","script":"katakana","origin":"platform","joker":{"reveal.kana":[{"id":"countries-katakana/america.candy","text":"アメ can mean candy or rain. America gets both. いいね.","status":"ship","trigger":{"wordIncludes":"アメリカ"},"when":["meaning"],"ja":["いいね"],"subj":"world"},{"id":"countries-katakana/america.rice","text":"Japan's short name for America means rice. Delicious. すごい.","status":"ship","trigger":{"wordIncludes":"アメリカ"},"when":["meaning"],"ja":["すごい"],"subj":"world"},{"id":"countries-katakana/canada.kana","text":"カナダ begins with カナ. Clearly your kind of country. とうぜん.","status":"ship","trigger":{"wordIncludes":"カナダ"},"ja":["とうぜん"],"subj":"you"},{"id":"countries-katakana/canada.village","text":"Canada comes from kanata, a word for village. Cozy. ほっこり.","status":"ship","trigger":{"wordIncludes":"カナダ"},"when":["meaning"],"ja":["ほっこり"],"subj":"world"},{"id":"countries-katakana/france.survey","text":"アンケート, the survey, came from French. Elegant paperwork. ほら.","status":"ship","trigger":{"wordIncludes":"フランス"},"ja":["アンケート","ほら"],"subj":"world"},{"id":"countries-katakana/germany.dutch","text":"ドイツ reached Japanese through Dutch traders. Well-travelled word. なるほど.","status":"ship","trigger":{"wordIncludes":"ドイツ"},"ja":["なるほど"],"subj":"world"},{"id":"countries-katakana/germany.arbeit","text":"アルバイト, a part-time job, comes from German. Hard-working word. さすが.","status":"ship","trigger":{"wordIncludes":"ドイツ"},"ja":["アルバイト","さすが"],"subj":"world"},{"id":"countries-katakana/germany.tsu","text":"ドイツ ends in ツ: last stroke falls from the top. きれい.","status":"ship","trigger":{"wordIncludes":"ドイツ"},"ja":["きれい"],"subj":"app"},{"id":"countries-katakana/italy.heritage","text":"Italy has the most World Heritage sites. Handsome country. みごと.","status":"ship","trigger":{"wordIncludes":"イタリア"},"when":["meaning"],"needs":["world.italy.mostHeritage"],"ja":["みごと"],"subj":"world"},{"id":"countries-katakana/spain.vowels","text":"Spanish vowels sound almost like Japanese ones. Easy listening. いいね.","status":"ship","trigger":{"wordIncludes":"スペイン"},"when":["meaning"],"ja":["いいね"],"subj":"world"},{"id":"countries-katakana/thailand.fish","text":"タイ is Thailand. たい is a lucky fish. Both めでたい.","status":"ship","trigger":{"wordIncludes":"タイ"},"when":["meaning"],"ja":["たい","めでたい"],"subj":"world"},{"id":"countries-katakana/india.aiueo","text":"The あいうえお order is based on Sanskrit. なるほど.","status":"ship","trigger":{"wordIncludes":"インド"},"when":["meaning"],"ja":["あいうえお","なるほど"],"subj":"world"},{"id":"countries-katakana/brazil.community","text":"Brazil has the largest Japanese community abroad. すごい.","status":"ship","trigger":{"wordIncludes":"ブラジル"},"when":["meaning"],"needs":["world.brazil.largestNikkei"],"ja":["すごい"],"subj":"world"},{"id":"countries-katakana/brazil.dakuten","text":"ブラジル wears dakuten twice. Extra sparkle. きらきら.","status":"ship","trigger":{"wordIncludes":"ブラジル"},"ja":["きらきら"],"subj":"app"},{"id":"countries-katakana/mexico.ink","text":"Mexico's kanji nickname means ink. A writer's country. ほら.","status":"ship","trigger":{"wordIncludes":"メキシコ"},"when":["meaning"],"ja":["ほら"],"subj":"world"},{"id":"countries-katakana/philippines.small","text":"フィリピン carries a small ィ. Tiny, and very important. だいじ.","status":"ship","trigger":{"wordIncludes":"フィリピン"},"ja":["だいじ"],"subj":"app"},{"id":"countries-katakana/philippines.islands","text":"Over seven thousand islands. Plenty of beaches. すてき.","status":"ship","trigger":{"wordIncludes":"フィリピン"},"when":["meaning"],"needs":["world.philippines.islands"],"ja":["すてき"],"subj":"world"},{"id":"countries-katakana/vietnam.kanji","text":"Vietnam once wrote with Chinese characters too. ほう.","status":"ship","trigger":{"wordIncludes":"ベトナム"},"when":["meaning"],"ja":["ほう"],"subj":"world"},{"id":"countries-katakana/portugal.pan","text":"パン, bread, came from Portuguese. A delicious import. おいしい.","status":"ship","trigger":{"wordIncludes":"ポルトガル"},"when":["meaning"],"ja":["パン",